Priority: 2
Area: Canvas
Status: done
Depends on: add-image-paste, add-pdf-page-import-and-recolor

Goal:
Make the eraser tool remove raster-backed canvas items such as pasted images and imported PDF page placements, not just strokes or vector items.

Context:
The user reports that the current eraser tool does not erase images. In this app, images and imported PDF pages are first-class canvas items, so the eraser should treat them as eraseable elements instead of leaving them as a special case that can only be removed through selection workflows.

Expected changes:

- inspect the current eraser hit-testing path in the canvas workspace
- extend erase hit-testing and deletion behavior to `image` items
- decide whether imported PDF page placements should follow the same erase path and implement that consistently
- keep erase behavior bounded to item removal; do not widen into selection redesign

Acceptance criteria:

- Using the eraser over a pasted image removes that image from the canvas.
- Using the eraser over an imported PDF page placement removes that item too, if the product treats it as an eraseable canvas element.
- Existing eraser behavior for strokes and shapes remains intact.
- `npm run build` and `cargo check --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml` pass.

Notes:

- Keep the behavior consistent with how the eraser already decides when an element is “hit”.
- If imported PDF pages need separate handling from normal images, document that clearly in the worker report.
